[size=5][b]Every mod key and controller button, rebindable in the vanilla menu.[/b][/size]

Rebind any mod key, even ones the mod never made rebindable, set key combinations, and rebind controller buttons, vanilla and modded, all in the game's own Key Bindings menu.

Mods that add keys usually leave them in an input file, in Mod Settings, or both, and many can't be changed in game at all. The game itself only lets you rebind keyboard keys. Unified Keybinds adds a section per mod to [b]Settings > Controls > Key Bindings[/b] with every action your installed mods add, and a controller view of the whole menu, so you can rebind everything in one place. The list is built from your installed mods each time the game starts.

[i]Formerly Native Mod Keybinds. Files and folders keep their names, so updating works as before.[/i]

[size=4][b]Supported keybind sources[/b][/size]

[table][tr][th]Status[/th]
[th]Keybind source[/th]
[th]Notes[/th]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url] input file, with or without overridableUI (for example [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/5208]Let There Be Flight[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/11765]Enhanced Vehicle System[/url])[/td]
